CSS can be used to adjust the alignment of HTML text by using the "text-align" property. This can be applied to different elements, such as headings, paragraphs, and lists, and can be set to left, right, center, or justify. For example:

```css
h1 {
  text-align: center;
}

p {
  text-align: justify;
}

ul {
  text-align: right;
}
```

In the above example, the "h1" headings will be centered, the "p" paragraphs will be justified, and the unordered lists "ul" will be aligned to the right.

